  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bae Systems Land and Armaments L P reported $1.1B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Bae Systems Land and Armaments L P received 31 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $34M. Bae Systems Land and Armaments L P obligations fell 51.3% year over year. Historical obligations show a rise through FY24 followed by declines: FY21 was $103M, FY22 was $604M, FY23 was $2.1B, FY24 was $2.3B, FY25 was $2.2B, and FY26 is $1.1B. Bae Systems Land and Armaments L P is concentrated in Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing, which accounts for $995M of FY2026 to date obligations, followed by Engineering Services at $39.5M and Motor Vehicle Gasoline Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $19.8M. Several NAICS markets show no obligations in the current year, including Current-Carrying Wiring Device Manufacturing and Other Electronic Component Manufacturing. The figures are contract obligations except where noted as total contract values in other tables.",
    "sections": [
